  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Nine double-regime prepositions",
   "texto": [
    "**An, auf, hinter, in, neben, über, unter, vor** and **zwischen** can be given either in the right direction or in the right direction. To indicate location and answer **wo? (¿dónde?)**, it is used dative: **Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch** (the book is on the table).",
    "The case does not depend on physical movement: it depends on whether a location is expressed or a destination / change of place. That's why **Ich laufe im Park** (running inside the park, location) and **Ich laufe in den Park** (running into the park, destination) is said."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The contractions",
   "texto": [
    "With dativa some are joined: **in dem** → **im** (in), **an dem** → **am** (next to), **bei dem** → **beim**, **von dem** → **vom**.",
    "Examples: **im Wohnzimmer** (in the living room), **am Fenster** (next to the window)."
   ]
